One-node limitations
Your current cluster has one node. It is enough for:
•
Pod lifecycle
•
Deployments
•
Services
•
Secrets and ConfigMaps
•
Health probes
•
Rolling updates
•
Helm
•
Ingress
•
Application routing
•
Basic autoscaling
•
Most debugging commands
It cannot realistically prove:
•
Node failure recovery
•
Cross-node networking
•
Pod anti-affinity across nodes
•
Topology spread
•
Multi-zone availability
•
Pod rescheduling after losing a worker
•
Real high availability